# Game: the Godot layer

This layer is a view. It owns no rules.

If a scene or node decides whether a word is valid, what something scores, or
what happens next, that logic is in the wrong place and belongs in
`WordRoguelike.Core`.

## Shape

One controller node holds the current `RunState` and an `IRandomSource`. Input
handlers build a `PlayerAction`, call into Core, store the returned state, and
feed the returned events into an animation queue. Nodes read state; they never
mutate it.

## Constraints

Strictness is relaxed here because Godot's source generators and its generated
`.csproj` emit warnings we do not control. That is not licence for sloppy code,
only for not failing the build on generated output.

C# Android export is experimental: arm64 and x64 only, linux-bionic Mono
runtime, no Android bindings. Prefer Godot's own APIs over .NET platform APIs.

Release builds may trim. Anything reflection-based (save serialization above
all) must be verified in a release build, not just a debug APK.

Godot regenerates this project's `.csproj` if it goes missing. The
`ProjectReference` to Core is committed and must be re-checked after any Godot
version upgrade.
